@page "/examples/scoped-widgets"
@rendermode InteractiveAuto
@inherits RfEventComponent

<ExampleHeader Title="Scoped widgets" Level="Complex" Mode="Interactive Auto">
    Several instances of the same widget, each with its own state and its own event scope, plus a
    page-level log that hears what bubbles out of them.
</ExampleHeader>

<div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-3">
    <form class="input-group w-auto" @onsubmit="AddList">
        <input class="form-control" placeholder="New list name…" @bind="_newList" @bind:event="oninput" />
        <button class="btn btn-outline-primary" type="submit" disabled="@string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_newList)">Add list</button>
    </form>
    <button class="btn btn-outline-danger" @onclick="ResetAllAsync">Reset all lists <small>(Route.Global)</small></button>
</div>

<div class="row g-3 mb-3">
    @foreach (var title in _lists)
    {
        <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4" @key="title">
            <TodoWidget Title="@title" OnRemove="() => _lists.Remove(title)" />
        </div>
    }
</div>

<ActivityLog />

<HowItWorks>
    <p><strong>Try it:</strong> add items to different lists, tick some, then use <em>Clear done</em> in one list and <em>Reset all lists</em>.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Each <code>TodoWidget</code> wraps its children in <code>&lt;StateScope TState="TodoListState" Name="widget"&gt;</code>. Every list gets its own store, and every child that asks for <code>TodoListState</code> resolves the nearest one.</li>
        <li><code>TodoInput</code> publishes <code>TodoAdded</code> with the default <code>Route.Bubble</code>: the widget scope, then up to the root, where <code>ActivityLog</code> listens.</li>
        <li><em>Clear done</em> publishes <code>ClearCompletedRequested</code> with <code>Route.Local</code>. Only that widget's <code>TodoItems</code> hears it, and the log's counter stays at 0.</li>
        <li><em>Reset all lists</em> publishes <code>ResetAllRequested</code> with <code>Route.Global</code>, which broadcasts from the root into every scope.</li>
        <li><code>TodoStats</code> uses a tuple selector <code>(Done, Total)</code>. Its render counter only moves when those numbers change.</li>
        <li>Removing a widget disposes its scope and store. Its subscriptions disappear with it.</li>
    </ul>
</HowItWorks>
